virglrenderer: Venus commands come where Vulkan allows them

What: vkr keeps a little state per command buffer: recording or not, the
render pass or rendering that is open (its subpass, colors and view mask,
cleared when it ends; the render pass and framebuffer by id and serial,
never by pointer), whether a graphics or a compute pipeline is bound,
conditional rendering. A command on a command buffer that does not record,
a draw outside a pass or without a graphics pipeline, a dispatch inside a
pass or without a compute pipeline, a clear outside a pass or of a color
attachment the subpass lacks, a pass begun inside another, a next subpass
past the last, a pass end without its begin, a next subpass or pass end
whose render pass or framebuffer the app destroyed meanwhile, a query in a
multiview pass past the pool's end for its views, a conditional rendering
end without its begin, vkEndCommandBuffer with a pass or conditional
rendering open, and the execution of a secondary that still records or does
not match the primary's pass end the app's context.
Why: KosmicKrisp (NDEBUG) ended on a draw or dispatch without a pipeline, on
a next subpass past the last and on a pass end without a begin (SIGSEGV,
end_subpass); MoltenVK with prefill on the same and on a draw outside a pass
(SIGSEGV at vkEndCommandBuffer). With a render pass destroyed while a pass
of it was open, vkr and Mesa's vk_render_pass read freed memory at the next
subpass (a crash once that memory is reused or overwritten).
Upstream: OmacVM policy (spec VUIDs), draft only.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-commands.c (the c-state- cases).

